<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    RuStore's download CDN (static-m.rustore.ru) switched to a certificate issued by the
    Russian Trusted Root CA (Ministry of Digital Development), which Android does not ship
    in its system trust store. Update checks kept working because the API host
    (backapi.rustore.ru) still uses an ordinary publicly-trusted certificate, but every
    download failed TLS validation.

    So: for rustore.ru only, trust the system CAs AND that root. Both anchors are required —
    verified against the live hosts: the API validates solely via the system store, the CDN
    solely via the Russian root.

    Deliberately NOT done: disabling certificate validation for RuStore (what some other
    updaters offer as "allow insecure requests"). This app installs APKs — accepting any
    certificate would let anyone on the network serve a forged package. Adding one extra
    trust anchor, scoped to one domain, keeps validation fully intact everywhere.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config>
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">rustore.ru</domain>
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
            <certificates src="@raw/rustore_ca" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
